{
  "_note": [
    "What each instrument's firmware can do, so the program does not have",
    "to ask. Consulted on connecting; anything not listed here is asked",
    "instead, and an entry that turns out to be wrong is corrected against",
    "the instrument and written to the log.",
    "",
    "'model' is matched against the second field of *IDN?, exactly.",
    "'firmware' is matched against the last field as a substring; '*'",
    "matches any version. The first matching entry wins.",
    "",
    "'filesystem' whether the firmware has a FILESYSTEM subsystem at all.",
    "'reader'     READFILE, PRINT, or null when a file's contents cannot",
    "             be read over GPIB.",
    "'can_write'  whether FILESYSTEM:WRITEFILE exists.",
    "'options'    the factory option codes this firmware actually reads.",
    "             An option missing here has no getter in the ROM, so the",
    "             instrument will never report it however its word is set.",
    "             Read out of the images by optionscan.py.",
    "'image'      first ten hex digits of the firmware image's SHA-256.",
    "             Rows sharing an image share a byte-identical binary.",
    "",
    "'evidence':",
    "  measured - checked on the instrument itself.",
    "  firmware - read out of that model's firmware image: the SCPI",
    "             keyword table decoded from the ROM, which says directly",
    "             whether READFILE and WRITEFILE exist. The method was",
    "             validated against the three instruments marked measured,",
    "             and reproduces all three exactly.",
    "",
    "Three generations, and the difference matters:",
    "  v2.x           no filesystem over GPIB at all",
    "  A and B series browse and download, never upload",
    "  C and D series everything",
    "",
    "An instrument not listed here still works - it is asked when it",
    "connects. This table only saves it being asked. A capabilities.json",
    "beside the program overrides the bundled one."
  ],
